# What must not be uploaded when `npm run deploy` ships this directory to Vercel.
#
# ── Why this file has to exist ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore. Without this file it skips only its own short list
# (.git, .next, node_modules, .env.local, .vercel …) and uploads everything else as the
# deployment's source. Read in the CLI itself (getVercelIgnore, vercel 60.1.3), not assumed.
#
# And `scripts/deploy.mjs` renames .git to .git-parked for the duration – so the CLI's own .git
# rule never applies, and without the line below the whole repository history went up with every
# deploy. So did fixtures/ (real client documents), testing/ and the 474 MB local document store.
# None of it was served, but all of it sat in the deployment's source files, which is client data
# copied somewhere it has no reason to be (ARC-005: send the least that is needed).
#
# Same reasoning as .dockerignore, which keeps the same things out of the container image.

# The repository history, under the name deploy.mjs parks it as.
.git-parked/

# Real client data and test packs (README: the repository stays private until anonymised).
fixtures/
testing/

# The local document store and local tooling – development only; production uses Blob.
.storage/
.e2e-tmp/
.claude/
.agents/
.qodo/
test-results/

# Secrets. The CLI already skips .env.local; nothing else of this kind belongs in a build either.
.env
.env.*

# CI, hooks and the browser suites – they drive a running server from outside; the build needs none.
.github/
.githooks/
checks/

# Documentation read in the repository, not built.
HANDOFF.md
PLATFORM.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
design/
docs/

# Loose documents at the root – the practice's own working papers get saved here (a BOQ review, a
# cost-comparison memo, a mapping workbook were, the day this was written). Nothing the build reads
# lives at the root in these formats, so none of them may go up, whatever they are called.
/*.md
/*.pdf
/*.xls
/*.xlsx
/*.xlsm
/*.csv
/*.doc
/*.docx
/*.ppt
/*.pptx
/*.zip
/*.dwg
/*.dxf
